From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:41:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] qwen3_5 cuda: run an image prompt through the looped
 decoder

The tower and the loop each had a receipt on this branch and nothing joined
them: vision checked the tower alone, and every prompt verb ran text. cuda.zig
now publishes the image prompt's Media, and tf-qwen35-cuda gains:

  tf-qwen35-cuda <model> image <ids file> <out> <tokens> <picture> [steps]

It opens the engine and the tower the way --vision does (Vision.open against
the model's own width), prepares the picture with core/qwen_vl, splices the
tower's rows at the prompt's placeholders through the same src/pos tables
cuda_prefill uses, and decodes greedily with the reply's rows rotated past the
image's positions. The decoder is whatever the checkpoint's geometry says,
including a looped range, so one run exercises image rows and the loop together.

Writes <out> (tokens as u32) and <out>.logits.bf16 (the prompt's last row).
Compiled and run on a GPU in the G-down window; nothing here is measured yet.
